# CODEOWNERS — Tier 2 path register
#
# `docs/engineering/agent-workflow.md` and `CLAUDE.md` both say Tier 2 paths are
# enforced "through CODEOWNERS, not memory". This file is that register.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR HERE
#
# It marks which paths a conformance review must read at full depth — invariant
# checklist, audit-event shape, authorization on every entry point, tenant scoping
# below the UI, point-in-time behaviour. It is a review-depth signal.
#
# WHAT IT MUST NOT BECOME
#
# Do NOT enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch ruleset. The only
# code owner is a human, and the merge policy in `agent-workflow.md` is explicitly
# that nobody clicks anything: a PR merges on green CI plus the independent-review
# check. Requiring code-owner approval would deadlock every Tier 2 pull request on
# the one person the workflow is designed to keep out of the loop.
#
# The founder's attention goes to Decision Requests and milestone demos, not diffs.
#
# TIERS
#
#   0  docs, config, dependency bumps                    CI only
#   1  ordinary feature code                             CI + one review pass
#   2  authorization, tenancy, versioning, effectivity,   CI + review pass +
#      approval, audit, evidence, content hashing         invariant tests cited
#
# Everything not matched below is Tier 1 by default.

